//!
//! Every suite uses seed 42, ten warm-up problems, coefficients in
//! -16384..=16384, and basic polynomials with 37..=50 requested terms and
//! maximum total degree 30. Uniform cases use minimum total degree 22; sharp
//! cases use minimum total degree 0 and exponentially skewed variable weights.
//! Problem numbers include the ten upstream warm-up problems.
//!
//! Percentile anchors use the conventional nearest-rank definition: sort all
//! 200 published rows by the Symbolica 2.2 / FLINT 3.5 runtime ratio, then take
//! rows `ceil(q * 200)` for q = 0.10, 0.50, and 0.90. These historical ranks
//! select reproducible inputs; they do not describe the performance of the
//! current workspace implementation.
//!
//! GCD inputs are reconstructed before measurement as a*g and b*g for
//! nontrivial cases, or a*b and c*d for trivial cases. Factorization inputs are
//! reconstructed as a*b. The SHA-256 values verify the expanded canonical
//! strings emitted by SymEngine 0.13.0: GCD hashing uses
//! left + newline + right + newline, and factorization hashing uses
//! input + newline.

